&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a submission for the &lt;a href="https://dev.to/challenges/https://tolerix.devhacktoberfest-week2-2026-10-12"&gt;Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge Week 2: Side Hustle&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I Built
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tolerix is a local-first preflight software built for laser cutting, CNC routing, and digital fabrication side hustles. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When running a custom fabrication side business (such as cutting acrylic wedding signs, personalized keychains, or wooden craft kits), customers send unstructured instructions via email, Etsy messages, or Instagram DMs. Along with these notes, they provide vector files (SVG or DXF). &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Too often, there is an expensive mismatch:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The customer requested a 120 x 80 mm tag, but the drawing file was exported at 100 x 60 mm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The vector design contains unclosed contours, causing the laser head to leave pieces half-cut.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The file has duplicate overlapping vectors, causing the laser to trace the same line twice, which chars wood or melts acrylic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The file exceeds the physical laser bed boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In custom manufacturing, running a bad file ruins expensive sheet stock ($15 to $50 per panel) and burns billable machine time. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tolerix solves this problem before the operator hits start on the machine. It pairs local, open-weight Gemma models with a deterministic vector geometry engine to compare what the customer asked for against what the vector file actually contains.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Demo
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Live Application: &lt;a href="https://tolerix.onrender.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://tolerix.onrender.com/&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


The Preflight Workflow
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;pre data-lang="mermaid"&gt;&lt;code&gt;flowchart LR
A[Customer Notes] --&amp;gt; B[Local Gemma Model]
B --&amp;gt; C[Structured Job Spec]
D[Customer Vector File] --&amp;gt; E[Deterministic Geometry Engine]
E --&amp;gt; F[Exact Physical Dimensions &amp;amp; Contours]
C --&amp;gt; G[Rule Auditor]
F --&amp;gt; G
G --&amp;gt; H[Evidence-Backed Preflight Report]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The operator pastes customer notes, drops the SVG design into the browser, and immediately receives a clear preflight audit highlighting discrepancies, open paths, duplicate lines, and dimensional mismatches.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Code
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The complete source code is available on GitHub:&lt;/p&gt;


