&lt;div class="markdown-heading"&gt;
&lt;h3 class="heading-element"&gt;On-Device Model &amp;amp; Hardware Settings&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://github.com/greenbugx/Tolerix/docs/settings.png"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Fgreenbugx%2FTolerix%2FHEAD%2Fdocs%2Fsettings.png" alt="Tolerix Workspace &amp;amp; Model Settings"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="markdown-heading"&gt;
&lt;h2 class="heading-element"&gt;Architecture&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tolerix operates on a strict local-first architecture. There is no remote backend, hosted database, cloud sync, or external API dependency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Frontend &amp;amp; App Shell:&lt;/strong&gt; React 19, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, React Router, TanStack Query, Zod.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Persistent Data Layer:&lt;/strong&gt; IndexedDB managed via Dexie for jobs, files, machine profiles, specifications, audit runs, and findings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Local Model Storage:&lt;/strong&gt; Browser Cache Storage API (&lt;code&gt;tolerix-models-v1&lt;/code&gt;) for streaming and caching verified LiteRT-LM model weights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Local AI Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; On-device WebGPU inference using &lt;code&gt;@litert-lm/core&lt;/code&gt; LiteRT-LM runtime…&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="gh-btn-container"&gt;&lt;a class="gh-btn" href="https://github.com/greenbugx/Tolerix" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;View on GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;h3&gt;


Architecture Stack
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Application Shell:&lt;/strong&gt; React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS v4&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Local AI Inference:&lt;/strong&gt; LiteRT-LM WebGPU runtime executing Gemma 2B and Gemma 4B on device&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Vector Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; svg-pathdata, analytical Bézier extrema calculus, affine transform matrix stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Storage &amp;amp; State:&lt;/strong&gt; Dexie (IndexedDB) for jobs, files, audit runs, and machine profiles; Cache Storage API for model weights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How I Built It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tolerix separates generative reasoning from mathematical precision. AI extracts intended parameters from noisy human text, while deterministic algorithms inspect geometric vectors.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;pre data-lang="mermaid"&gt;&lt;code&gt;graph TD
subgraph Browser Client [100% Local Browser Sandbox]
subgraph AI Layer [LiteRT-LM WebGPU]
M1[Gemma 2B / 4B Weights] --&amp;gt; M2[Requirement Extraction]
M2 --&amp;gt; M3[Quantity, Dimensions, Material, Thickness, Operations]
end
subgraph Geometry Layer [Deterministic Engine]
G1[SVG / Path Parser] --&amp;gt; G2[2D Affine Matrix Accumulation]
G2 --&amp;gt; G3[Bézier Extrema &amp;amp; Arc Bounds Calculus]
G3 --&amp;gt; G4[Normalized Path &amp;amp; Duplicate Detection]
end
subgraph Storage Layer [IndexedDB &amp;amp; Cache API]
S1[(Dexie DB: Jobs, Files, Audits)]
S2[(Cache API: Verified Model Weights)]
end
subgraph Audit Engine [Preflight Validation]
M3 --&amp;gt; A1[Rule Auditor]
G4 --&amp;gt; A1
A1 --&amp;gt; A2[High / Med / Low Findings]
A2 --&amp;gt; A3[Printable HTML &amp;amp; Structured JSON Reports]
end
end&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


Feature Matrix: What Works and What Does Not
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Component&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What Works&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What Does Not Work (Current Limitations)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gemma AI Extraction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Runs Gemma 2B and Gemma 4B on device via WebGPU. Extracts target dimensions, material names, quantities, and cut/engrave operations. Includes regex heuristic fallback when offline without weights.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Does not run on machines lacking WebGPU support or GPUs with under 4 GB VRAM.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Geometry Engine&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Computes exact mathematical bounds for quadratic and cubic Bézier curves and elliptical arcs. Correctly handles 2D affine transforms (nested groups, rotation, scale, skew) and non-zero viewBox origins.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Does not deduce non-vector properties like actual sheet thickness or laser wattage from 2D coordinates; these remain flagged as unverified for human review.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duplicate Path Detection&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Compares normalized coordinate sequences and reversal-invariant trajectories to catch duplicate cut paths.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Does not automatically merge intersecting paths; it detects and flags them for the operator.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;File Security&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Strict element allowlist. Rejects scripts, event handlers, foreignObject, iframe, external entity declarations (XXE), and remote HTTP references. Enforces 50 MB limits.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;DXF parsing currently supports basic 2D planar contours; complex 3D meshes or ACIS blocks are unsupported.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting &amp;amp; Persistence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Persists jobs, specs, vector Blobs, and findings in IndexedDB via Dexie. Exports printable HTML reports and JSON audit logs with strict HTML escaping.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Does not sync across devices or offer cloud backup by design. All data stays local to the workstation.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why Does Open Innovation Matter?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open innovation is what makes Tolerix viable as a real tool for small shops.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Zero Marginal Cost for Small Business:&lt;/strong&gt; A small laser engraving business operating on Etsy or at weekend craft markets cannot afford recurring API subscription tiers or usage fees per preflight check. Open-weight models like Gemma run on hardware the maker already owns, costing zero dollars in cloud API bills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Total Workshop Privacy and IP Protection:&lt;/strong&gt; Makers handle proprietary product designs, unreleased prototypes, and custom corporate logos. Sending these customer files to third-party proprietary AI cloud APIs introduces privacy risks and intellectual property concerns. With open-weight models and local execution, customer data never leaves the workshop workstation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Offline Reliability in the Garage:&lt;/strong&gt; Laser cutters and CNC routers are frequently installed in garages, basements, or industrial park units where Wi-Fi is spotty or nonexistent. Tolerix runs completely offline from local cache, so production never halts because the internet went down.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No Vendor Lock-In:&lt;/strong&gt; Proprietary APIs change prices, alter deprecation schedules, and introduce rate limits. Open weights give builders stability and permanence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

