&lt;h3&gt;


3. Synchronize metadata flags automatically
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of a separate script, I embedded the flag update into the main pipeline (&lt;code&gt;scripts/publish_all.js&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/p&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;
js
// scripts/publish_all.js
const { execSync } = require("child_process");
const fs = require("fs");
const path = require("path");

function updateMetadata(flags) {
const metaPath = path.join(
__dirname,
"..",
"content/2026/10/14/content-automation/metadata.json"
);
const meta = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(metaPath, "utf8"));
Object.assign(meta, flags);

---

*Part of my [Build in Public](https://dev.to/zaerohell) series — sharing the real process of building SaaS projects from Playa del Carmen, México.*

*Repo: `zaerohell/content-automation` · 2026-10-15*

\#playadev #buildinpublic
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As developers, we spend a lot of time building websites, optimizing metadata, and making sure our projects look good when shared on social media.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But there's one small problem: &lt;strong&gt;how do you check what your website's link preview actually looks like before sharing it?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are tools that help with this, but some put useful features behind paid plans. For a simple task like previewing a URL, I wanted to build a free alternative.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So, I created &lt;strong&gt;OG Link Preview&lt;/strong&gt;!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;🔗 &lt;strong&gt;Try it here:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://oglinkpreview.vercel.app/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://oglinkpreview.vercel.app/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


💡 What is OG Link Preview?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;OG Link Preview is a web tool designed to help developers inspect how a URL may appear when shared online.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It focuses on Open Graph metadata, which helps platforms generate rich link previews containing information such as:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Title&lt;/strong&gt; — The title displayed in the preview.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Description&lt;/strong&gt; — A short summary of the page.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Preview image&lt;/strong&gt; — The image associated with the shared link.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Metadata&lt;/strong&gt; — Information that helps social platforms understand your page.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


🎯 Why did I build it?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I wanted a straightforward tool that developers could use without needing to pay just to check their link previews.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sometimes, small tools solve everyday problems and save developers time. That's the idea behind this project.&lt;/p&gt;

